And the reason is because the market very quickly auctioned away from lower prices.

239
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:14,520
But because it was done within the already established range,

240
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:18,240
it might not have appeared as just a traditional tail

241
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:20,100
where we have single prints.

242
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:24,700
And then in the last example, we have a market open tail.

243
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:31,100
As you can see, the market opens towards the lower bound and very quickly, you know, the market navigates higher.

244
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:36,800
Nice, confident up move in prices as we see initiative from the open.

245
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:44,400
So those are the three types of excess that you're likely to see, you know, in volume profiling.

246
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:51,000
We're now going to begin our in-depth discussion of the volume point of control.

247
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,600
We briefly spoke about this in Module 1.

248
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:56,700
I showed you how to identify this in the volume profile.

249
00:15:56,900 --> 00:16:00,252
But now we're going to take a look at why the volume

250
00:16:00,252 --> 00:16:02,487
profile is important to be able to understand

251
00:16:02,487 --> 00:16:06,398
and interpret and what it can mean over a period of a trading session.

252
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,163
Now, the first thing is the volume point of control,

253
00:16:10,163 --> 00:16:13,926
or VPOC, as it's better known and as people will

254
00:16:13,926 --> 00:16:20,699
often name it, is the price at which the most volume in a trading session can be found.

255
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:23,743
So that price over a period of a day where

256
00:16:23,743 --> 00:16:25,264
the most volume is transacted

257
00:16:25,264 --> 00:16:27,698
is known as the volume point of control.

258
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:33,000
In basic sense, it is the price that is... the most trading activity within a trading session.

259
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:41,000
Now note, markets that are in balance tend to retest this point of control whilst they remain in balance.

260
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:46,400
So straight away, bang, the market opens and you've identified opening in balance.

261
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:53,400
There is a very high probability that we will retest the previous day's volume point of control.

262
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:57,424
Again, knowing this little bit of information can aid you

263
00:16:57,424 --> 00:17:01,148
in developing a very early strategy just based on where

264
00:17:01,148 --> 00:17:04,499
the market is opening in terms of trade location.

265
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:07,652
Now, the point of control can also act

266
00:17:07,652 --> 00:17:12,999
as a strong reference point in markets that are slowly accepting value higher or lower.

267
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,497
So what we mean by that is that when we see a

268
00:17:16,497 --> 00:17:18,828
trending day or when we see initiative taken

269
00:17:18,828 --> 00:17:23,199
in the market, what we tend to see is a developing volume point of control.

270
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:26,760
So it may start at the low end of the day, but

271
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:29,133
then as price rises, we see the volume

272
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:32,099
point of control continues to rise over the entire session.

273
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:36,430
Now, traditionally, as a rule of thumb, in a trend day, the

274
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:40,399
volume point of control will constantly be moving with the trend.

275
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:44,500
And more often than not, we'll literally be closing.

276
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:47,055
The volume point of control will be at either the

277
00:17:47,055 --> 00:17:51,399
high of the day in an uptrend or at the low of the day in a downtrend.

278
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:56,800
Then the more pronounced the VPOC, the more significant it becomes.

279
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:00,000
So a lot of the time we could see in a volume profile,

280
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:03,633
maybe five or six or seven different prices could have

281
00:18:03,633 --> 00:18:06,299
been the volume point of control and the

282
00:18:06,299 --> 00:18:08,632
volume difference between those prices is very

283
00:18:08,632 --> 00:18:10,298
marginal in that case it's

284
00:18:10,298 --> 00:18:13,298
slightly less pronounced however if you know we have

285
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:19,500
a very pronounced volume point of control where that price is the obvious you know price that

286
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:25,800
traded the most volume, well that makes it more pronounced and more likely to be retested.

287
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:30,900
Then we can observe the volume point of control in two ways.

288
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:35,546
One is the static point of control from the previous section and

289
00:18:35,546 --> 00:18:40,499
the second is the new point of control being formed on the current day.

290
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:43,920
So straight away, what we're trying to look at here is that

291
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:47,340
we need to lean on the previous day's volume point of control

292
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:51,900
but then equally we need to also focus on the current day's volume point of control.

293
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:57,371
And note, the movement of the point of control over a day

294
00:18:57,371 --> 00:19:02,799
gives us vital clues as it measures where volume is being distributed relative to trade location.

295
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:07,185
So what we should typically see is that the volume point of

296
00:19:07,185 --> 00:19:10,042
control as a kind of almost rule of

297
00:19:10,042 --> 00:19:15,399
thumb should in theory be within the value area or where trade is being accepted.

298
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:20,452
A lot of the time we can see price very quickly navigating

299
00:19:20,452 --> 00:19:25,600
away from the value area, but the point of control stays firmly put.

300
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:29,400
And when we have this, we do sometimes tend to get some very aggressive.

301
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:33,995
snapback type trades as the market moves very

302
00:19:33,995 --> 00:19:39,999
quickly in terms of price away from where fair value is actually accepted.

303
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:44,154
And then if prices move aggressively away from the point of control

304
00:19:44,154 --> 00:19:47,199
and cannot facilitate trade away from the point of control,

305
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:53,400
there's a very high probability the market will trade back towards the accepted price.

306
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:57,800
A little bit what I was talking about in that previous sentence.

307
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:01,000
So that's the volume point of control.

